Overview:

The ProgramMemory module is designed to store and manage lines of code associated with specific line numbers, similar to how BASIC programs are structured. 
It uses a std::map to maintain the order and quick access of lines, allowing features like adding, updating, deleting, listing, and renumbering lines. 
The module also supports saving and loading program lines from files using a system interface, enabling persistent storage.



